      "writtenOn": "2023-12-20T21:35:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is that actually possible? This function is only called to get the binder thread object for the current thread which should not have been added by any other thread. aosp/404738 made the C driver have the same end result for this error case, but that was a simplification instead of a requirement. It would be equally valid to return an error here. The C version handles the allocation path with a single extra tree traversal over the old global lock version, but this rust version seems to use two extra traversals. Why can\u0027t the rb tree insert function handle the error case instead?",
      "revId": "9c704ab0ccbcb4cbc74db11128c9d81f053b183a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
